<%- include('partials/head', { page: page, title: title, cfg: cfg }) %>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Players</h2>
      <div class="muted" id="playersRange">—</div>
    </div>

    <div class="card about" id="playerNamesHint" hidden>
      <p>
        <b>The server is not exposing its player list right now.</b> The monitor can still see how
        many players are online, but not who they are, so while someone is connected a
        “Hidden player” card is shown below instead of a named one. Name tracking needs the
        GameSpy4 query protocol, which Bedrock Dedicated Server (the official software) does not
        support; on PocketMine-MP / Nukkit enable the query option in the server config to get names.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid four">
      <div class="card mini"><span>Players seen</span><b id="pSeen"><span class="skeleton chip"></span></b></div>
      <div class="card mini"><span>Online now</span><b id="pOnlineNow"><span class="skeleton chip"></span></b></div>
      <div class="card mini"><span>Joined today</span><b id="pJoinedToday"><span class="skeleton chip"></span></b></div>
      <div class="card mini"><span>Left today</span><b id="pLeftToday"><span class="skeleton chip"></span></b></div>
    </div>

    <div class="pgrid" id="playersGrid">
      <div class="card pcard">
        <div class="pcard-head"><i class="dot"></i><span class="skeleton chip" style="width: 90px"></span></div>
        <div class="skeleton num" style="margin-bottom: 10px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton" style="display: block; height: 8px; border-radius: 99px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton chip" style="margin-top: 12px"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card pcard">
        <div class="pcard-head"><i class="dot"></i><span class="skeleton chip" style="width: 90px"></span></div>
        <div class="skeleton num" style="margin-bottom: 10px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton" style="display: block; height: 8px; border-radius: 99px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton chip" style="margin-top: 12px"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card pcard">
        <div class="pcard-head"><i class="dot"></i><span class="skeleton chip" style="width: 90px"></span></div>
        <div class="skeleton num" style="margin-bottom: 10px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton" style="display: block; height: 8px; border-radius: 99px"></div>
        <div class="skeleton chip" style="margin-top: 12px"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card about" id="playersEmpty" hidden>
      <p>
        No players seen yet. The monitor records every player it catches online — they will appear
        here the first time they join while the app is watching.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
